<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI3152-IPC-SHUTDOWN-UNBOUNDED-JOIN>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AI3152-IPC-SHUTDOWN-UNBOUNDED-JOIN" ;
  triage:title "Unbounded worker.join() in daemon worker pool shutdown paths risks indefinite shutdown hang" ;
  triage:description "ConnectionWorkerPool::shutdown (crates/atm-daemon/src/local_ipc_transport.rs:373) and DispatchWorkerPool::shutdown (crates/atm-daemon/src/local_ipc_transport/request_worker.rs:182) both call worker.join() with no deadline/timeout. A genuinely wedged worker can block daemon shutdown indefinitely." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "daemon-shutdown" ;
  triage:severity "Blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "workspace" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-08-02T00:30:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AICH-S13 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-08-02T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI3152-IPC-SHUTDOWN-UNBOUNDED-JOIN/FIX-M5-1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI3152-IPC-SHUTDOWN-UNBOUNDED-JOIN/FIX-M5-2> ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "2" ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-08-02T21:15:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:progressNote "M5-ADMISSION-QA-3: fixed at d1f3ad0f. Both call sites now route through the shared join_workers_with_timeout (local_ipc_transport/admission.rs:29-60) with LOCAL_WORKER_JOIN_DEADLINE=250ms; on timeout it returns AtmError::daemon_lifecycle_wedge and drops the JoinHandle without calling .join(), genuinely detaching a wedged worker rather than blocking. Deterministic zero-deadline test worker_join_timeout_detaches_a_wedged_worker (admission.rs:110-139) proves the bound without repeating the QA-2-caught release-before-shutdown anti-pattern. Confirmed independently by req-qa, arch-qa, and quality-mgr direct read. Consistent with https_transport.rs's join_tracked_dispatches/HTTPS_TIMEOUT precedent. NOTE: the same unbounded-join pattern was found unfixed elsewhere in the daemon (peer_drain_coordinator.rs, local_tcp_transport.rs, post_commit_work.rs) via workspace sweep -- filed separately as AI3152-JOIN-UNBOUNDED-RECUR (Blocking). The join_workers_with_timeout primitive itself also duplicates two sibling implementations -- filed separately as AI3152-JOIN-TIMEOUT-DUPLICATE-IDIOM (Important). This record covers only the original two occurrences and is closed on that narrow scope." ;
  triage:progressNote "M5-ADMISSION-POSTMERGE-REVIEWERBACKED (integrate/phase-ai-31-33 @ c9ba04d9): reconfirmed fixed post-merge. Reviewer-backed recheck (req-qa, arch-qa, ruthless-boundary-qa independently corroborating; rust-qa-agent test/fmt pass but killed before full clippy completion) plus quality-mgr direct git/grep verification found the fix intact on the merged commit, matching origin/integrate/phase-ai-31-33. No regression." .

